    "title": "Flint Creek Range highest peak is Mount Powell | Around The Web | wvnews.com",
    "text": "Mount Powell, at 10,168 feet, rises in the Flint Creek Range of southwestern Montana. It is the loftiest pinnacle of this compact mountain range.\nVery rugged is the best way to describe the Flint Creek country, and ascending any peak within is a challenge, but well worth it. Reaching the summit of Powell is no exception. It is a 14-mile roundtrip and involves a very precipitous final push. The panorama from the top of Powell opens views to mountain ranges and valleys in all directions.",
